 FAST ENERGY REGION                                               7443 1451   68
 Authors: R. Capote, A. Trkov, E. Soukhovitskii                   7443 1451   69
                                                                  7443 1451   70
 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               7443 1451   71
                                                                  7443 1451   72
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                7443 1451   73
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               7443 1451   74
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             7443 1451   75
                                                                  7443 1451   76
 Available experimental data were interpreted  using              7443 1451   77
 nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-2.19b35 by                    7443 1451   78
 M. Herman et al [He01, He02]. This code integrates               7443 1451   79
 into a single system a number of important modules               7443 1451   80
 and features:                                                    7443 1451   81
                                                                  7443 1451   82
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 7443 1451   83
   coupled-channels (ECIS03 by J. Raynal)                         7443 1451   84
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    7443 1451   85
   HRTW width fluctuation correction                              7443 1451   86
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                7443 1451   87
   TRISTAN by H. Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                      7443 1451   88
 - Exciton model with angular momentum coupling                   7443 1451   89
   (code DEGAS by E. Betak and P. Oblozinsky) that                7443 1451   90
   represents a good approximation to the DSD model               7443 1451   91
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      7443 1451   92
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 7443 1451   93
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                7443 1451   94
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   7443 1451   95
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                7443 1451   96
   discrete transitions                                           7443 1451   97
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL-2 library [Ri03]              7443 1451   98
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                7443 1451   99
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               7443 1451  100
   and gamma strength functions  based on the RIPL-2              7443 1451  101
   library [Ri03]                                                 7443 1451  102
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              7443 1451  103
   EXFOR/CSISRS library                                           7443 1451  104
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A. Trkov)                    7443 1451  105
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 7443 1451  106
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                7443 1451  107
   PrePro codes by R. Cullen                                      7443 1451  108
 - Checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                        7443 1451  109
 - Support for NJOY                                               7443 1451  110
                                                                  7443 1451  111
