 *** ENDRESS - Merging source and resonance ENDF files            7443 1451  575
             Source ENDF W186_ib21g.t0                            7443 1451  576
          Resonance ENDF ..\resonance\W186_ib8forAndrej.end       7443 1451  577
                                                                  7443 1451  578
RESOLVED RESONANCE PARAMETERS (L. Leal, ORNL, January 2008)       7443 1451  579
 Starting from the resonance parameter data in the IRDF-2002      7443 1451  580
 library, small adjustments were made to reproduce the thermal    7443 1451  581
 capture cross section of 38.09 barns and the resonance integral  7443 1451  582
 of 483.4 barns as closely as possible. This ratio 12.69 is in    7443 1451  583
 good agreement with the value 12.59+/-0.22 from the Kayzero      7443 1451  584
 database for neutron activation analysis [1].                    7443 1451  585
                                                                  7443 1451  586
RESOLVED RESONANCE PARAMETERS (IRDF-2002)                         7443 1451  587
    Resolved MLBW resonance parameters up to  8.5 keV  were based 7443 1451  588
on data from ref.[2-3]. Spins of resonances, which were not iden- 7443 1451  589
tified, have been assigned by taking into account 2*J+1 law  and  7443 1451  590
approximate linear growth of the number of levels with given spin 7443 1451  591
and parity from energy. Average gamma-widths 0.05 eV (L=0 and L=1)7443 1451  592
were assigned to those resonances, widths for which were absent.  7443 1451  593
Fictitious resonances were added in the energy region 4 - 8.5 keV 7443 1451  594
to obtain  the average capture cross section values  observed  in 7443 1451  595
the experiments [4],[5],[6],[7].                                  7443 1451  596
                                                                  7443 1451  597
UNRESOLVED RESONANCE PARAMETERS (IRDF-2002)                       7443 1451  598
    Unresolved resonance parameters in  the region  8.5 - 100 keV 7443 1451  599
were evaluated  with using 'EVPAR' code (Hauser-Feshbach-Moldauer 7443 1451  600
statistical model)[8]. They were calculated from optimized fit to 7443 1451  601
the measured capture [5,6,7,9,10] and total [11,12] cross sections7443 1451  602
data.  Average resolved resonance  parameters  have been  used as 7443 1451  603
zero approximation.  Contribution of  F-wave in the energy region 7443 1451  604
30 - 100 keV given as smoothed background cross section in File 3.7443 1451  605
                                                                  7443 1451  606
RESONANCE COVARIANCE DATA (L. Leal, ORNL, Jan 2008)               7443 1451  607
The procedure used to generate the resolved covariance data       7443 1451  608
with the SAMMY code is as follow:                                 7443 1451  609
 a) Retrieve best set of available resonance parameters.          7443 1451  610
 b) Convert the resonance parameters into the Reich-Moore form.   7443 1451  611
 c) Generate "experimental" cross sections for total, scattering, 7443 1451  612
    and capture cross sections with the NJOY code, for use as     7443 1451  613
    "experimental data" in SAMMY.                                 7443 1451  614
 d) Assign a global "experimental" uncertainty to the             7443 1451  615
    "experimental data." The uncertainties used were based on     7443 1451  616
    uncertainty in the thermal capture cross section and          7443 1451  617
    uncertainty in the capture resonance integrals.               7443 1451  618
 e) Run SAMMY code with the option to generate                    7443 1451  619
    resonance-covariances retroactively.                          7443 1451  620
 f) Convert the resonance-covariance results from SAMMY into      7443 1451  621
    the ENDF format for file 32 and MT=151.                       7443 1451  622
                                                                  7443 1451  623
The resulting resonance parameters and covariance were used in    7443 1451  624
the calculations of average cross sections and uncertainties.     7443 1451  625
The calculations were done with SAMMY, ERRORJ, and PUFF-IV codes. 7443 1451  626
The results of these three codes agreed very well.                7443 1451  627
                                                                  7443 1451  628
